  "Question": "When \\(y=A\\sin(\\omega t+\\varphi)+b\\) is used to describe a periodic phenomenon, what does \\(b\\) represent?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Highest point",
    "B": "Period",
    "C": "Equilibrium position",
    "D": "Starting time"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(b\\) is the center of the upward and downward oscillation. The maximum is \\(b+|A|\\), and the minimum is \\(b-|A|\\).",
